Patch: 0003-deterministic-plonk.patch
Applies to: native/vendor/dungeonmaker-2.05/DungeonMaker.cpp (after 0001 and 0002)
What: PlonkDownStuff initializes startX/startY before their first read in both sections
  for MOBs in the open (labyrinth and dungeon), so the branch the code means is taken,
  and SortRooms sorts with std::stable_sort, so rooms of equal size keep their creation order.
Why: Reading the uninitialized startX is undefined behaviour that differs per compiler, and
  std::sort orders rooms of equal size differently in libc++ and libstdc++; both would make
  the placed MOBs and treasure platform-dependent (spec sections 5.3 and 7.2). Neither
  function runs unless entities are requested, so existing cells do not change.
Date: 2026-10-31
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

--- a/DungeonMaker.cpp	2026-10-31 19:59:37.754620160 +0100
+++ b/DungeonMaker.cpp	2026-10-31 19:59:37.757221554 +0100
@@ -3682,7 +3682,7 @@
 
 void alifegames::DungeonMaker::SortRooms()
 {
-  sort(Rooms.begin() , Rooms.end() , RoomComp() );
+  stable_sort(Rooms.begin() , Rooms.end() , RoomComp() );  //patch 0003: equal sizes keep creation order, see native/patches/
 }
 
 void alifegames::DungeonMaker::PlonkDownStuff()
@@ -4067,7 +4067,7 @@
       int plonkY = 1 + ( rand()%(dimY-3) );
       IntCoordinate Test( plonkX , plonkY );
       //now make a starting direction
-      int startX , startY;
+      int startX = 1 , startY = 0;  //patch 0003: defined start direction, see native/patches/
       if( (rand()%100) < 50 )
 	startX = 0;
       else
@@ -4140,7 +4140,7 @@
       int plonkY = 1 + ( rand()%(dimY-3) );
       IntCoordinate Test( plonkX , plonkY );
       //now make a starting direction
-      int startX , startY;
+      int startX = 1 , startY = 0;  //patch 0003: defined start direction, see native/patches/
       if( (rand()%100) < 50 )
 	startX = 0;
       else
